WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.400
The National Academy of Sciences says that Grand Isle is affected by a storm once every 2.5 years.

2
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.700
Let me tell you . . . There's a picture right behind there, right behind your head right there.

3
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.780
My father lost everything in 1965.

4
00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:17.020
That's me right there with the little white pants on top.

5
00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:19.780
That was 1965 for Betsy, you see me standing there,

6
00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:23.760
and I remember my dad telling me that I looked at him and said, "What we going to do?"

7
00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:26.440
He told my brother and I, he said, "We going to go ahead and rebuild."

8
00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:29.320
I said, "Dad, we don't have no insurance or nothing like that."

9
00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:30.360
He said, "It doesn't matter.

10
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:31.720
We're going to make a living here.

11
00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:33.880
We make our living, this is where we're raised at.

12
00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:36.220
I know what I'm doing to get back in the waters."

13
00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:44.280
And one of the sayings that my dad said, forty years later came back and I had to use the same saying.

14
00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:50.540
People were coming back on the island after Betsy, and my dad said, "Just remember, it's material things.

15
00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:51.580
We can replace that.

16
00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:55.220
You didn't lose your family you didn't lose your wife, you didn't lose your kids."

17
00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:59.000
I didn't know forty years later after Katrina would hit,

18
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:05.180
that I had to look at this young woman and look at her and look at her kids and look at her husband and say . . . First thing is,

19
00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:09.420
she'll look at me and she'll tell me, "Mr. David, I don't have anything left."

20
00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:13.720
And I know she doesn't, but I can't lie to her, but I'll tell her, "Don't worry about that.

21
00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:15.100
It's material things.

22
00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:19.620
You got your kids, you got your husband, I promise you I will get you back."

23
00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:30.320
And I guess being a native boy, dealing with the natives on the island, you know, we're used to that type of living.

24
00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:33.340
We're not asking the government to come in.

25
00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:38.320
We know they're going to come in and help us, but when you're a bunch of Cajun and natives,

26
00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:40.480
you're going to help each other, and that's what we did for Katrina.
